and people weren't willing to
do it so for their negligence,

00:28:20.598 --> 00:28:22.534 align:start size:97% position:3%
for their stupidity, they
should take a haircut as well.

00:28:22.534 --> 00:28:24.703 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, obviously the
shareholders are wiped out.

00:28:24.703 --> 00:28:26.304
That's capitalism.

00:28:26.304 --> 00:28:29.774 align:start size:84% position:16%
If you don't have a
consequence for stupid

00:28:29.774 --> 00:28:32.777 align:start size:88% position:13%
and risky behavior, well
you just get stupider

00:28:32.777 --> 00:28:34.245
and more risky behaviors.

00:28:34.245 --> 00:28:36.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
So the way the Fed has
done this, and by the way,

00:28:36.481 --> 00:28:39.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you think they would
have bailed out depositors

00:28:39.517 --> 00:28:41.986 align:start size:84% position:16%
if those depositors
were, oh I don't know,

00:28:43.722 --> 00:28:48.727 align:start size:88% position:13%
oil drillers, refineries
or gun manufacturers?

00:28:50.128 --> 00:28:51.362
So no, these were all the
little woke businesses

00:28:51.362 --> 00:28:52.897
in Silicon Valley.

00:28:52.897 --> 00:28:54.933 align:start size:97% position:3%
They were doing everything,
you know, green energy.

00:28:54.933 --> 00:28:57.602
You know, these businesses
probably never made money.

00:28:59.437 --> 00:29:00.672 align:start size:88% position:13%
- [Dave] Right,
they're tech start ups.

00:29:00.672 --> 00:29:01.606 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Were probably
going through cash

00:29:01.606 --> 00:29:03.742
sooner than they needed to.

00:29:03.742 --> 00:29:06.111
So again, all the way
around, the way the Fed

00:29:06.111 --> 00:29:08.113 align:start size:84% position:16%
has handled this
has been mismanaged,

00:29:08.113 --> 00:29:11.182
and what it'll probably do
is it will probably hasten

00:29:11.182 --> 00:29:14.152 align:start size:88% position:13%
the next banking crisis
and make it worse.

00:29:14.152 --> 00:29:15.653
Good job.

00:29:15.653 --> 00:29:17.088
- Is that sort of what the
Fed wants, do you think?

00:29:17.088 --> 00:29:18.990
Again, going to sort
of the maliciousness

00:29:18.990 --> 00:29:20.825
versus incompetence
thing, to me it seems

00:29:20.825 --> 00:29:22.160
like the Fed always
wants to get bigger.

00:29:22.160 --> 00:29:23.962
The machine just wants
to get bigger, right?

00:29:23.962 --> 00:29:26.197
So okay, the more big
things that we have

00:29:26.197 --> 00:29:28.533
that are too big to fail, we'll
just keep making them bigger

00:29:28.533 --> 00:29:30.869
and then there'll be one bank
and it'll be in this town.

00:29:30.869 --> 00:29:32.670 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I mean, yeah, there
are people saying

00:29:32.670 --> 00:29:36.374
this is just the game
plan, the strategy,

00:29:36.374 --> 00:29:39.577
to move toward a central
bank digital currency,

00:29:39.577 --> 00:29:41.679
which would give me
cause for concern.

00:29:43.348 --> 00:29:47.185
You know, it's long past
arguing whether or not

00:29:47.185 --> 00:29:48.887 align:start size:88% position:13%
we should have a
Federal Reserve or not.

00:29:48.887 --> 00:29:50.255
I think that's been decided.

00:29:50.255 --> 00:29:52.090
They're not going to go away.

00:29:52.090 --> 00:29:55.560
But you're far better off
with decentralized power.

00:29:55.560 --> 00:29:58.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're far better off with
a lot of smaller banks.

00:29:58.029 --> 00:30:00.331
Now, you do need some big banks,

00:30:00.331 --> 00:30:02.167 align:start size:88% position:13%
do the big international
transactions

00:30:02.167 --> 00:30:04.402
and do things that,
big businesses too.

00:30:04.402 --> 00:30:08.173 align:start size:88% position:13%
Some things only big
businesses can do, okay?

00:30:08.173 --> 00:30:09.707
But what I've seen, for example,

00:30:09.707 --> 00:30:12.143
my plastics manufacturing plant.

00:30:12.143 --> 00:30:15.513 align:start size:97% position:3%
When I started that business
in late '70s, early '80s,

00:30:15.513 --> 00:30:18.817 align:start size:97% position:3%
we probably had a couple
hundred potential customers.

00:30:18.817 --> 00:30:22.620
My guess is that's shrunken
down to about 12 major ones

00:30:22.620 --> 00:30:24.088 align:start size:84% position:16%
because everything's
consolidated.

00:30:24.088 --> 00:30:27.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
All these little
individual manufacturing,

00:30:27.292 --> 00:30:29.494
plastics manufacturers,
thermoformers and stuff,

00:30:29.494 --> 00:30:31.729
you know, great
little businesses

00:30:31.729 --> 00:30:34.265 align:start size:97% position:3%
for little towns and
stuff, they get gobbled up,

00:30:34.265 --> 00:30:36.334 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that manufacturing
goes from there

00:30:36.334 --> 00:30:38.136
into a much larger plant.

00:30:38.136 --> 00:30:39.637
That's not good.

00:30:39.637 --> 00:30:42.540
It's small businesses that
are the engines of innovation

00:30:42.540 --> 00:30:45.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
in our economy and provide
the kind of competition

00:30:45.343 --> 00:30:47.946
you really need in a
competitive system.

00:30:47.946 --> 00:30:50.148
So I don't like to see
all this consolidation.

00:30:50.148 --> 00:30:52.517
I think that's something
that the federal government

00:30:52.517 --> 00:30:55.253
does have a role to play
in terms of anti-trust.

00:30:55.253 --> 00:30:59.157
I think we need to re-think and
re-work the anti-trust laws.

00:30:59.157 --> 00:31:00.725 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's all around
benefiting the consumer,

00:31:00.725 --> 00:31:02.861
and that makes sense,
but how do you handle

00:31:02.861 --> 00:31:05.897
these big tech social media
giants where it's all free?

00:31:05.897 --> 00:31:09.467
So it's almost impossible
to prove consumer harm,

00:31:09.467 --> 00:31:11.336
but I think you can
prove societal harm.

00:31:11.336 --> 00:31:13.071 align:start size:84% position:16%
When you start seeing
the cooperation

00:31:13.071 --> 00:31:15.106
with government officials
to censor information.

00:31:15.106 --> 00:31:17.709
I mean, something has
to be done about that.

00:31:17.709 --> 00:31:20.712
But you've got Democrats won't
help us legislatively on that

00:31:20.712 --> 00:31:23.848
because it plays
to their advantage.

00:31:23.848 --> 00:31:25.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Is that the weird thing,
that we find out things

00:31:25.984 --> 00:31:28.987 align:start size:97% position:3%
like the Twitter files where
we know without question

00:31:28.987 --> 00:31:32.190 align:start size:97% position:3%
100% proof positive the
government was coordinating

00:31:32.190 --> 00:31:34.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Twitter and Facebook,
Psaki even admitted it

00:31:34.192 --> 00:31:36.961
a year and a half ago, but
nobody cared about Facebook,

00:31:36.961 --> 00:31:39.464
that they were censoring people

00:31:39.464 --> 00:31:40.765
at the behest of the government.

00:31:40.765 --> 00:31:42.934
It's a violation of
the First Amendment.

00:31:42.934 --> 00:31:44.669
That's basically it.

00:31:44.669 --> 00:31:47.138
But the show just goes on.

00:31:47.138 --> 00:31:48.373
- Well, you're seeing
the mainstream media

00:31:48.373 --> 00:31:50.008
screaming about that, right?

00:31:50.008 --> 00:31:50.875
Oh, I guess we're not.

00:31:50.875 --> 00:31:51.709
- No, exactly.

00:31:51.709 --> 00:31:53.011
- That's the problem.

00:31:53.011 --> 00:31:55.313
So we know about it,
Fox News covers it,

00:31:55.313 --> 00:31:56.781 align:start size:84% position:16%
a couple of
conservative outlets,

00:31:56.781 --> 00:31:59.984 align:start position:0%
but by and large the vast
majority of the American public

00:31:59.984 --> 00:32:02.754
is completely unaware
of what happened there

00:32:02.754 --> 00:32:04.889 align:start position:0%
because they're being distracted
on their little news feeds

00:32:04.889 --> 00:32:08.826 align:start size:88% position:13%
by the Kardashians or
whatever you're getting.

00:32:08.826 --> 00:32:10.228
- Is that the push and
pull that you always

00:32:10.228 --> 00:32:11.696
have to deal with as a senator,

00:32:11.696 --> 00:32:13.698 align:start size:97% position:3%
that you probably could
get more done on the ground

00:32:13.698 --> 00:32:16.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
just focusing on
Wisconsin, but you're part

00:32:16.768 --> 00:32:18.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the federal machine too
obviously as a senator,

00:32:18.903 --> 00:32:22.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it's almost distracting
from where you can get

00:32:22.373 --> 00:32:23.574
concrete things done?

00:32:23.574 --> 00:32:25.910 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well again, the things
I want to get done

00:32:25.910 --> 00:32:28.813
are reduce the burden of
the federal government.

00:32:28.813 --> 00:32:30.949 align:start size:84% position:16%
So when people come
into my office,

00:32:30.949 --> 00:32:32.784
if you're looking for
a government handout,

00:32:32.784 --> 00:32:36.621 align:start size:97% position:3%
probably go to the Democrat
senator from Wisconsin.

00:32:36.621 --> 00:32:39.357
If you're looking to help get
the government off your back,

00:32:39.357 --> 00:32:40.858
you've come to the right office.

00:32:40.858 --> 00:32:45.863 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I'm here, you
know, trying to uphold

00:32:47.065 --> 00:32:48.533
the vision of our
founding fathers.

00:32:48.533 --> 00:32:50.068 align:start size:97% position:3%
Yeah, we need some government,
you can't live in anarchy,

00:32:50.068 --> 00:32:52.170
you can't live in chaos, so
you need some government,

00:32:52.170 --> 00:32:53.671
but it needs to be limited.

00:32:53.671 --> 00:32:56.607
Because our founders, they
came from tyrannical regimes.

00:32:56.607 --> 00:32:59.577
They realized as government
grew, their freedom recedes,

00:32:59.577 --> 00:33:02.880
and let's face it, freedom
is the essential ingredient

00:33:02.880 --> 00:33:04.349
in America.

00:33:04.349 --> 00:33:08.653 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's the freedom that people
use to dream and aspire

00:33:08.653 --> 00:33:10.722
and build and create this
marvel we call America.

00:33:10.722 --> 00:33:12.190
It's not big government.

00:33:12.190 --> 00:33:14.692 align:start size:84% position:16%
Big government
crushes those dreams.

00:33:14.692 --> 00:33:16.861
Big government takes
away that freedom.

00:33:18.296 --> 00:33:21.899
So my goal here isn't to bring
home the bacon to Wisconsin,

00:33:21.899 --> 00:33:24.102 align:start size:97% position:3%
my goal is to shrink the size
of the federal government

00:33:24.102 --> 00:33:28.539 align:start position:0%
so Wisconsinites can aspire
and dream and build and create.

00:33:28.539 --> 00:33:30.742
- Let's do a couple of
other of the big ones.

00:33:30.742 --> 00:33:32.944 align:start size:88% position:13%
This Ukraine situation,
which we are,

00:33:32.944 --> 00:33:35.713
I think it's around
$160 billion now.

00:33:35.713 --> 00:33:37.815
It's weapons, it's
not a declared war,

00:33:37.815 --> 00:33:39.217 align:start size:81% position:19%
but at some point,
in my opinion,

00:33:39.217 --> 00:33:42.987 align:start position:0%
if you're funding a war
forever, you're kind of at war.

00:33:42.987 --> 00:33:45.490
I think you're pretty much
in the same spot as that.

00:33:45.490 --> 00:33:46.924
What do you make of this?

00:33:46.924 --> 00:33:48.226
Is there any off ramp?

00:33:48.226 --> 00:33:50.561 align:start size:88% position:13%
Every week we have
spokesmen telling them,

00:33:50.561 --> 00:33:52.296
no, there'll be no negotiation.

00:33:52.296 --> 00:33:54.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's all very
bizarre, to say the least.

00:33:54.966 --> 00:33:56.334 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I'll give you a little
more fulsome answer

00:33:56.334 --> 00:33:57.902
because I think it requires one.

00:33:59.370 --> 00:34:00.838
Yeah, I was chairman of
the European Subcommittee

00:34:00.838 --> 00:34:02.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
on Senate Foreign
Relations, ranking member.

00:34:02.573 --> 00:34:04.142 align:start size:81% position:19%
I've probably been
over to Ukraine

00:34:04.142 --> 00:34:06.077
as much as just about
any of my colleagues.

00:34:06.077 --> 00:34:07.779 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was at Poroshenko's
inauguration.

00:34:07.779 --> 00:34:10.248
I was the only member of
Congress at Zelenskyy's.

00:34:12.283 --> 00:34:13.851
Zelenko's the doctor that ...

00:34:15.153 --> 00:34:16.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, so it was
Zelenskyy's inauguration.

00:34:16.454 --> 00:34:17.655
I thought he was the real deal.

00:34:17.655 --> 00:34:19.590
I know the Ukrainian people are.

00:34:19.590 --> 00:34:22.860
They want to shed themselves
of the legacy of corruption.

00:34:22.860 --> 00:34:26.898 align:start size:97% position:3%
And to describe it for you,
his prosecutor general,

00:34:26.898 --> 00:34:29.233
when I was over there,
he said let me describe

00:34:29.233 --> 00:34:30.668
corruption in Ukraine.

00:34:30.668 --> 00:34:33.438 align:start size:97% position:3%
We have something like 22,000
prosecutors in Ukraine.

00:34:33.438 --> 00:34:36.074
We don't pay them well,
but they live like kings.

00:34:37.241 --> 00:34:39.310
I mean, that's the
endemic corruption.

00:34:39.310 --> 00:34:41.679
Okay, so the Maidan,
that was a scream.

00:34:41.679 --> 00:34:44.582
We want what you
have in the West.

00:34:44.582 --> 00:34:46.517
I mean, I have nothing but
sympathy for that, right?

00:34:46.517 --> 00:34:49.287 align:start size:84% position:16%
I have nothing but
sympathy for a country

00:34:49.287 --> 00:34:50.855
and for its people
that are invaded

00:34:50.855 --> 00:34:54.792
by an evil war criminal,
and that's who Putin is.

00:34:54.792 --> 00:34:56.594
Okay, so I don't want to
give any aid or comfort

00:34:56.594 --> 00:34:59.697
to Putin whatsoever,
and I want to support

00:34:59.697 --> 00:35:01.466 align:start size:81% position:19%
the courageous
people of Ukraine.

00:35:03.034 --> 00:35:06.938
But I think there
was certainly a way

00:35:06.938 --> 00:35:08.673 align:start size:88% position:13%
of preventing that
invasion to begin with,

00:35:08.673 --> 00:35:11.476
but not under Biden
obviously, okay?

00:35:12.944 --> 00:35:16.881
So once invaded, once the one
opportunity we might have had

00:35:16.881 --> 00:35:20.084
when Russia felt a resistance

00:35:20.084 --> 00:35:22.086
because of the courage
of the Ukrainian people

00:35:22.086 --> 00:35:24.555
and the support of the
West, which I supported

00:35:24.555 --> 00:35:28.359
that first tranche because
partly we had to replenish

00:35:28.359 --> 00:35:30.862 align:start size:84% position:16%
our munitions, that
the Commander in Chief

00:35:30.862 --> 00:35:32.730
can just deplete our stockpile,

00:35:32.730 --> 00:35:36.334 align:start size:84% position:16%
so we had to replace
those as well.

00:35:36.334 --> 00:35:39.737 align:start size:97% position:3%
There was a moment in time,
it was a glimmer hope,

00:35:39.737 --> 00:35:41.038
where maybe Russia
would say, whoa,

00:35:41.038 --> 00:35:42.607
we bit off way more
than we can chew.

00:35:42.607 --> 00:35:46.344
Let's return back
and let's end this.

00:35:46.344 --> 00:35:47.912
But that was quite a while ago.

00:35:49.080 --> 00:35:50.815
Now the reality of
the situation is

00:35:52.150 --> 00:35:54.385
you don't have a
fair fight here.

00:35:54.385 --> 00:35:57.355
Putin can continue to
send in cruise missiles

00:35:57.355 --> 00:36:00.525 align:start size:88% position:13%
and bomb population
centers, infrastructure.

00:36:00.525 --> 00:36:03.661
I mean, this war just
continues to grind on,

00:36:03.661 --> 00:36:06.397
and just more and more
of Ukraine is destroyed.

00:36:06.397 --> 00:36:09.033
Now, both sides are
losing individuals,

00:36:09.033 --> 00:36:12.436
but certainly when I've asked
people in the State Department

00:36:12.436 --> 00:36:15.273
well, what's the public
opinion polls in Russia?

00:36:15.273 --> 00:36:17.408 align:start size:84% position:16%
They're highly
supportive of the war.

00:36:17.408 --> 00:36:18.609
Well, why wouldn't they?

00:36:18.609 --> 00:36:20.845
They've got Putin's propaganda.

00:36:20.845 --> 00:36:23.414
They're not getting
their cities bombed.

00:36:23.414 --> 00:36:26.083 align:start size:84% position:16%
So it's a completely
unfair fight.

00:36:26.083 --> 00:36:28.786 align:start size:84% position:16%
There's no way Putin
gives up on this.

00:36:28.786 --> 00:36:29.720
There's no way.

00:36:29.720 --> 00:36:31.455
It's existential for him.

00:36:31.455 --> 00:36:36.460
So it's a reality I hate,
but at some point in time,

00:36:37.628 --> 00:36:39.363
everybody's gonna have
to face the reality.

00:36:39.363 --> 00:36:43.234
Every day that this goes
by, the eventual outcome

00:36:43.234 --> 00:36:47.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
just gets worse and worse
and worse and worse.

00:36:47.138 --> 00:36:48.606
It doesn't get better.

00:36:48.606 --> 00:36:50.208 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So when you hear our State
Department or even Biden

00:36:50.208 --> 00:36:53.044 align:start size:88% position:13%
saying the Ukrainians
don't have to negotiate,

00:36:53.044 --> 00:36:54.312 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is what they've
said repeatedly

00:36:54.312 --> 00:36:55.546
over the last couple of weeks.

00:36:55.546 --> 00:36:56.781
I mean, what do
you make of that?

00:36:58.249 --> 00:36:59.617
- How does this get better?

00:37:00.818 --> 00:37:02.753
Give me a scenario in
terms of where we turn

00:37:02.753 --> 00:37:05.323
this thing around and you
end up with a better result

00:37:05.323 --> 00:37:06.857
than what you have right now.

00:37:06.857 --> 00:37:09.460 align:start size:88% position:13%
If you were to just
stop fighting right now,

00:37:09.460 --> 00:37:12.530
how does it get better
by continuing to fight?

00:37:12.530 --> 00:37:13.965
Again, it's a horrible reality.

00:37:13.965 --> 00:37:15.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hate saying this because
I don't want to give

00:37:15.566 --> 00:37:17.868
any aid and comfort to Putin.

00:37:17.868 --> 00:37:20.538
I guess I would just ask
everybody, including Putin,

00:37:20.538 --> 00:37:23.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
right now this is a
lose-lose-lose situation,

00:37:23.507 --> 00:37:27.011
other than maybe
China wins, okay?

00:37:28.412 --> 00:37:30.481
But I guess I would
just ask everybody

00:37:30.481 --> 00:37:34.485 align:start size:84% position:16%
to kind of temper
what they're thinking.

00:37:36.954 --> 00:37:39.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
We shouldn't be
contemplating going to war

00:37:40.825 --> 00:37:43.661
with either Russia or China.

00:37:43.661 --> 00:37:45.263
There's no good outcome on that.

00:37:47.531 --> 00:37:48.899
- [Dave] They're kind of
coming together right now.

00:37:48.899 --> 00:37:51.102
- There is no good
outcome on this.

00:37:51.102 --> 00:37:54.138
I mean, we've got to recognize
the reality of the situation.

00:37:54.138 --> 00:37:58.542
I mean, China is growing
their military, their navy.

00:37:59.710 --> 00:38:01.679
They get a lot more
bang for the buck,

00:38:01.679 --> 00:38:03.214
what they spend on military.

00:38:05.182 --> 00:38:08.953 align:start size:97% position:3%
So again, it's maybe not a
reality I like to contemplate,

00:38:08.953 --> 00:38:11.355
but it's a reality
you have to accept.

00:38:11.355 --> 00:38:13.224
- So I mentioned that I saw
you a couple of weeks ago

00:38:13.224 --> 00:38:14.859
at this blueprint
event in Florida

00:38:14.859 --> 00:38:16.294 align:start size:84% position:16%
that Governor
DeSantis was holding,

00:38:16.294 --> 00:38:18.929 align:start size:97% position:3%
